config.source:
URGENT = ["crash", "data loss", "lost data", "security", "password", "payment", "charged",
          "outage", "cannot log in", "can't log in", "corrupt", "deleted"]
SAMPLE = {
    "title": "App crashes when saving a workflow",
    "body": "Every time I press save the window closes and my last edits are gone.",
    "reporter": "sample",
}


def main(input_data):
    d = input_data if isinstance(input_data, dict) and input_data.get("title") else SAMPLE
    title = str(d["title"]).strip()[:200]
    body = str(d.get("body", ""))[:4000]
    text = (title + " " + body).lower()
    hits = [w for w in URGENT if w in text]
    return {"title": title, "body": body, "reporter": str(d.get("reporter", "unknown")),
            "urgent": bool(hits), "signals": ", ".join(hits)}

config.prompt:
This bug report was flagged urgent because it mentions: {{ $.signals }}.

Title: {{ $.title }}
Details: {{ $.body }}

Give (1) the most likely causes, (2) the first three things to check, (3) who should be told. Under 150 words.
